  and slowly i'll understand more and more  of it i won't necessarily understand it  all but it doesn't matter when i'm tired  of it whether i understand 30 50 70  i move on to something else because the  words that i'm having trouble  understanding and the phrases they're  going to show up again and of course now  that we have link which we didn't really  have we didn't have korean on link six  years ago or whenever it was seven or  eight years ago i tend to use link so  i'm going to give you a bit of a  demonstration of what i do when i um  approach  you know or try to understand whether  listening or reading  texts that are too difficult for me  which is something that i feel we have  to do i should add i don't believe in  this that you're always going to read  something that only has five three  percent new words you'll be forever  acquiring the necessary vocabulary i  feel you have to attack more difficult  texts listen to them read them  accept the fact that they're going to  remain fuzzy for a long long time but in  this way gradually you're training your  brain  to understand and get used to the new  language  so this is where i  come when i open up link you'll notice  that  i'm on the learn page as it's called the  first question you know people ask me  well how can you listen to stuff that  you don't understand well first of all  here there are a number of courses  recommended to me and i can choose to go  to something that's intermediate which  has 187 new words for me or  this is intermediate 1 with 254 new  words or  there are there's even advanced stuff  that i've tried here  uh intermediate or beginner so useful  expressions for beginners so i can  choose just how hard i want to make  things for myself and  and i vary it this one here for example  is is low intermediate almost high  beginner i've spent some time there  there's no more new words there i don't  necessarily understand at all  um  but uh here's one that i noticed that  has nine roses so other people like this  course  so before i open it up here i should  also point out a few other things here  we have the learn page is where you  learn exchange is where you can ask for  help find tutors have your writing  corrected find friends and this is just  a handy list of the various things that  you can do it's sort of a shortcut these  are the various lessons that i've been  studying or i can post a request to have  something corrected or i can join a  conversation i can import a lesson from  the internet or i can review my  vocabulary you'll notice here that my  avatar which is kind of an indication of  my progress  shows that i've become more active than  i was  i've been able to acquire a bunch of  artifacts for my avatar and here is sort  of a  progress snapshot which shows that i've  been linking pretty heavily compared to  my targets  but i don't do a lot of flash carding so  i haven't yet moved my links to learned  links are my saved words but i will be  doing so  and we'll get into that later on i can  also flash card the  most frequently used words that i have  saved so far but let's leave all of that  and let's go now  into  uh one of the lessons  all right so we'll open this one here  because it's new to me  so this is you know talking to random  people so we'll open one lesson in this  course  and uh so you'll see right away right  off the bat that there are a lot of blue  words and these are all the words here  that are new to me that i haven't seen  before in fact there's only 17 words  here that i've previously saved  and that is partly because i've been  listening to a lot of  sort of politics and economics and that  kind of thing whereas here we have more  of a casual  conversation  so the question is you know obviously if  i listen to this i'm not going to  understand it very well  pretty hard for me so the question is  how can you deal with  listening to stuff that you don't  understand well  i might listen to it once not understand  very